# Quality Control of Medicinal Products

## Project Team

Research staff of the Department of Pharmaceutical and Toxicological Chemistry named after A.P. Arzamastsev, Institute of Pharmacy named after A.P. Nelyubin, Sechenov University

## Project Description

## Project Aim

Development, validation, and implementation of a comprehensive set of analytical methods for the quality control of medicinal products, ensuring objective assessment of the authenticity, purity, and quantitative content of pharmaceutical substances and finished dosage forms in accordance with the requirements of the State Pharmacopoeia of the Russian Federation (SP RF), the Eurasian Economic Union (EAEU), and ICH.

## Key Objectives

- Analysis and harmonization of quality control approaches for medicinal products with the requirements of the SP RF, EAEU, and ICH;
- Development and optimization of identification and quantitative determination methods using HPLC, GC, UV spectrophotometry, titrimetry, mass spectrometry, and chromatography-mass spectrometry;
- Validation of methods against the following parameters: specificity, linearity, accuracy, precision, range of application, limit of detection and limit of quantification, and robustness;
- Control of related impurities, residual solvents, microbiological purity, dissolution, and dose uniformity;
- Study of medicinal product stability and establishment of shelf life;
- Development of rapid and screening methods for the detection of substandard, falsified, and counterfeit medicinal products;
- Preparation of draft pharmacopoeial monographs, regulatory documentation, and methods for testing laboratories;
- Piloting and implementation of the developed methods in quality control practice.

## Key Scientific Publications on the Project

- Shulga N.A., Gegechkori V.I., Gorpinchenko N.V., Smirnov V.V., Dementyev S.P., Ramenskaya G.V. Development of Ketoprofen Impurity A (1-(3-Benzoylphenyl)ethanone) as a Certified Reference Material for Pharmaceutical Quality Control // Pharmaceuticals. — 2025. — Vol. 18, No. 1. — P. 59. https://doi.org/10.3390/ph18010059
- Gegechkori V.I., Shatilina A.A., Shchepochkina O.Yu., Panchenko O.V., Kuzina V.N. Application of proteomic analysis for identification of the pharmaceutical substance pancreatin in developing a reference standard // Pharmacy. — 2023. — Vol. 72, No. 7. — P. 23–29. https://doi.org/10.29296/25419218-2023-07-03
